<section class="focus-pillars wrap wide" aria-label="The three fundamental conjectures">
  {% for focus in site.focusAreas %}
    <article id="focus-{{ focus.key }}" class="focus-pillar focus-pillar--{{ focus.key }} reveal">
      <div class="focus-pillar-number" aria-hidden="true">{{ focus.numeral }}</div>
      <div class="focus-pillar-body">
        <p class="kicker">{{ focus.eyebrow }}</p>
        <h2>{{ focus.label }}</h2>
        {% if focus.key == 'integration' %}
          <p class="focus-pillar-thesis">The framework begins with a process claim: a self is not a finished object but a repeatedly renewed act of integration. Differentiation is therefore not merely loss. It supplies what the next integration must gather.</p>
          <p>Written schematically rather than as established dynamics, the proposal is \(I_{n+1}=\mathcal{R}(I_n,D_n)\): a renewed integration \(I_{n+1}\) depends on an earlier integration and its differentiating remainder. The equation names the conjecture; it does not yet provide a physical law.</p>
        {% elif focus.key == 'splice' %}
          <p class="focus-pillar-thesis">At each density threshold, the Rankin Skeletal Splice proposes a fork: one half continues into the next density while one half returns. The fixed points \(-1,0,1\) form the “skeleton” against which that recurrent division is imagined.</p>
          <p>Once the splice rule is assumed, its idealised population count is mathematically checkable: \(P_n=F_{n+2}-1\). What remains conjectural is the promotion from a recurrence model to a mechanism of nature.</p>
        {% else %}
          <p class="focus-pillar-thesis">Return requires geometry. Part III asks whether seams, inversions and temporal antipodes can model re-entry without treating infinity as a distant wall or a place reached by travelling far enough.</p>
          <p>The Möbius identification \((x,0)\sim(1-x,1)\) is established topology. Using it as an analogue for cosmic or temporal return is the speculative move—and the archive keeps that distinction visible.</p>
        {% endif %}
        <p class="focus-equation" aria-label="Representative expression">\[{{ focus.equation }}\]</p>
        <a class="focus-primary-link" href="{{ focus.url }}">Begin with the central study <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>

        <section class="focus-programme" aria-labelledby="focus-programme-{{ focus.part }}">
          <header class="focus-programme-head">
            <p class="kicker">Integrated research programme</p>
            <h3 id="focus-programme-{{ focus.part }}">Part {{ focus.part }} · {{ focus.partTitle }}</h3>
            <p>{{ focus.partNote }}</p>
          </header>
          <ol class="focus-programme-documents">
            {% for item in focus.documents %}
              <li>
                <a data-focus-programme-document href="{{ item.url }}">
                  <span class="focus-programme-code">{{ item.code }}</span>
                  <span class="focus-programme-copy">
                    <strong>{{ item.label }}</strong>
                    <small>{{ item.kind }} · {{ item.status }}</small>
                    <span>{{ item.note }}</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="focus-programme-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section class="focus-synthesis reveal" aria-labelledby="focus-synthesis-title">
  <div class="wrap wide focus-synthesis-grid">
    <div class="focus-synthesis-copy">
      <p class="kicker">The minimal map</p>
      <h2 id="focus-synthesis-title">Integration differentiates. The splice routes. The seam returns.</h2>
      <p class="lede">That sequence is the framework’s shortest complete statement.</p>
      <p>It can be read at three levels: as a philosophical account of self-renewal; as a recursive mathematical model with conditional consequences; and, most ambitiously, as a proposed bridge to gravity, time and cosmology. The first may be argued, the second can be audited, and the third still requires definitions, dynamics and discriminating evidence.</p>
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/skeletal-splice/">Examine the proposed mechanism</a>
    </div>
    <div class="focus-sequence" aria-label="Integration to splice to return sequence">
      <div><span>01</span><strong>Integrate</strong><small>A provisional unity forms.</small></div>
      <b aria-hidden="true">↓</b>
      <div><span>02</span><strong>Differentiate</strong><small>The unity cannot remain static.</small></div>
      <b aria-hidden="true">↓</b>
      <div><span>03</span><strong>Splice</strong><small>Continuation and return divide.</small></div>
      <b aria-hidden="true">↓</b>
      <div><span>04</span><strong>Cross the seam</strong><small>Return becomes possible without an edge.</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

